{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/663909-types-of-artistry-for-changeling-usually-overlooked","id":663909,"title":"Types of artistry for Changeling usually overlooked?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-13T22:48:45-07:00","id":663909,"title":"Types of artistry for Changeling usually overlooked?","content":"I am looking for different types of art you don't normally consider. Most of what we hear about in Changeling is poetry, sculpting, painting, and singing. <br /> <br /> I am actually looking for something that pushes the boundaries of what we consider art and yet still works. The Satyr Kithbook lists sex as an art that you can achieve Rapture from, so I guess seduction is also a valid art to Muse or Rapture with. Bullying to, now that I think about it. Also, perhaps engineering, particularly for battle bots? What non traditional arts can you think of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T04:46:04-07:00","id":664097,"title":"","content":"The first edition corebook specifically introduced changeling cliques like the Zoetropes (movie fans), Olympians (body builders), Terpsichorians (dancers) . . . and . . .shoot, I've forgotten the name. Epicureans (maybe?), who focused on cooking. In the <i>Immortal Eyes</i> novels, we even saw Leigh (a.k.a. Dame Eleighnara) achieve Rapture from preparing a new fish recipe.<br /> <br /> Elsewhere, in <i>Freeholds and Hidden Glens, </i>there's &quot;Florist Primeval&quot;. A florist/botanical garden (and changeling freehold), they're known for producing Glamour with particularly skilled bouquets, gardens and other floral arrangements.<br /> <br /> There were also canon examples of gaining Glamour from storytelling (both prose and oral), making jewelry . . . Really, any activity that involves human inspiration. And even many of the &quot;conventional&quot; choices have odd manifestations - one red cap kept himself in Glamour with junkyard/trash sculptures, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/663909-types-of-artistry-for-changeling-usually-overlooked#post663909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . . Also, perhaps engineering, particularly for battle bots? What non traditional arts can you think of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems likely, given the whole moon landing incident . . . And in Goblin Town, a steampunk freehold under New York City, the &quot;chief engineer&quot; is second only to the ruler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  typo 09-14-2015, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T09:54:38-07:00","id":664509,"title":"","content":"Making/setting off fireworks, tattooing/body-piercing/body-modification, LARPing, playing certain types of video games...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T10:54:38-07:00","id":664546,"title":"","content":"Anything that requires creativity and inspiration would work as a source of Glamour - computer programming, hot rodding, writing mathematical theorems, extreme sports, etc.<br /> <br /> By the same token, though, any of those could also be banal if they're reduced to blind rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T22:05:12-07:00","id":665387,"title":"","content":"Doesn't Fool's Luck have a Gamemaster as a suggested Changeling archtype.. though that might be abit meta.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T03:49:13-07:00","id":665505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/663909-types-of-artistry-for-changeling-usually-overlooked?p=665387#post665387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't Fool's Luck have a Gamemaster as a suggested Changeling archtype.. though that might be abit meta.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about the supplement, but the actual freehold is noted for its annual (Glamour-producing) riddle contest<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: For those who haven't seen <i>Changeling </i>yet - The Fool's Gambit is a Boston-based tavern (and freehold), centered around the stump of the original Liberty Tree, which is popular with anti-sidhe/anti-nobility changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 09-15-2015, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T07:51:35-07:00","id":665696,"title":"","content":"These things are also easier to achieve than a classical masterpiece, which I think is important, since Glamour is a scarce resource in the game. I'd encourage players to think outside the box: construction, fashion, hairdressing, hat-making, drag, DJing. You could also argue that non-creative/generative activities that nevertheless inspire people might also count in the right circumstances: a really important touchdown, an act of heroism, perhaps a really witty or insightful comment. Some of these might not garner much Glamour, but you might award it once in a blue moon to reward exceptional roleplaying that adds to the sense of the mythic and magnificent in the otherwise mundane world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T13:37:38-07:00","id":666040,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I just remembered something. <a href=\"http://www.worldsuperheroregistry.com/world_superhero_registry_gallery.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.worldsuperheroregistry.co...ry_gallery.htm</a><br /> <br /> Though I wonder how they get Glamour out of it. Is it like reaping faith, or do you get spontaneous shots of glamour as stories of you grow?<br /> <br /> Edit: Musing, you probably can inspire by being a sidekick to a dreamer, rapture, you probably just need to be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 09-15-2015, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}